    "stem": "Hemant knows the number of taps and the time to fill a fixed tank are inversely proportional. With $5$ taps the job takes $12$ hours. He needs the time when $8$ taps work on the same tank.\n\nWhich plan is correct?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Keep the product constant: $5\\times12=8\\times t$, so $t=\\dfrac{60}{8}=7.5$ hours.",
      "B": "The constant product is only a label, so ignore the fixed tank and pick any time.",
      "C": "Scale time the same way as taps: $t=12\\times\\dfrac{8}{5}=19.2$ hours, as if the tank size need not stay fixed.",
      "D": "The answer is $12$ hours because $12$ is the only time printed in the stem."
    },
